course: dictionary
lesson: 15080
title: Ripened: ready over time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ripened is the past form of ripen, which means to become ready. When fruit ripens, it changes over time: it grows softer, sweeter and often changes colour. «The green bananas ripened on the windowsill.» The bananas became ready to eat, and it happened slowly, over days.
explain: Ripened can also mean that something was developed fully over time. «Her plan ripened over many months.» The plan did not change in a moment. It grew fuller and better as the months went by. Look for clue words such as over time, slowly, grew and waited.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The apples ripened on the tree» becomes «The apples became ready to eat on the tree», and that still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Ripened is the past form of the verb ripen.
fact: «Ripened» means became ripe, ready to eat or ready to harvest.
fact: «The time was ripe» means the right moment had come.
fact: Phrases such as «sun-ripened» and «ripened on the vine» show that fruit grew ready in sunshine or on the plant.
fact: Ripened can also be an adjective, describing something that has become fully ready or developed.
exercise: «The green bananas ripened on the windowsill.» What does ripened mean here? | *Became ready to eat, soft and sweet | Turned into a bird | Were thrown away | Stayed green forever
exercise: What does «the time was ripe» mean? | The clock was broken | It was very hot outside | The fruit was rotten | *The right moment had come
exercise: «Her plan ripened over many months.» What does this suggest? | *The plan grew fuller and better over time | The plan was thrown away quickly | The plan was finished in one minute | The plan was written in red ink
test: «The sun-ripened tomatoes were warm and sweet.» What does sun-ripened tell you? | The tomatoes were cooked in a pan | The tomatoes were green and sour | The tomatoes were stolen from the shop | *The tomatoes grew ready in the sunshine
test: Which word is the past form of ripen? | ripen | ripening | *ripened | ripens
exam: «The cheese ripened in a cool cellar for six months.» What does ripened mean here? | *Developed fully over time, becoming ready | Melted in the sun | Was cut into small pieces | Went bad and smelly
